{%- comment -%}
  HLT One - reassurance line directly under the cart drawer's Checkout button.

  Usage (from snippets/cart-drawer.liquid, inside .cart__ctas, after the
  checkout <button>):
    {%- render 'hlt-cart-drawer-trust' -%}

  HONESTY NOTE
  ------------
  Bloom's equivalent line reads "30,000+ five-star reviews". HLT One has no
  verified review count, so no review number or rating is shipped here: an
  unverifiable count on a live storefront would be a false advertising claim.

  The default text is "Secure checkout" - the same reassurance the cart page
  already makes (sections/main-cart-footer.liquid, `secure_text`), and one that
  is true of any Shopify checkout. "Free delivery" was deliberately NOT used as
  the default, because this store quotes "Shipping: calculated at checkout" and
  "Tracked delivery across Singapore", which do not support an unconditional
  free-delivery claim.

  The stars are behind `drawer_trust_stars`, which defaults to false, so no
  rating renders unless the merchant deliberately switches it on and supplies
  wording they can stand behind. Clearing the text hides the line entirely.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign hlt_trust_text = settings.drawer_trust_text -%}

{%- if hlt_trust_text != blank -%}
  <p class="hlt-drawer-trust">
    {%- if settings.drawer_trust_stars -%}
      <span class="hlt-drawer-trust__stars" role="img" aria-label="Rated 5 out of 5 stars">
        {%- render 'hlt-icon', name: 'star', size: 13 -%}
        {%- render 'hlt-icon', name: 'star', size: 13 -%}
        {%- render 'hlt-icon', name: 'star', size: 13 -%}
        {%- render 'hlt-icon', name: 'star', size: 13 -%}
        {%- render 'hlt-icon', name: 'star', size: 13 -%}
      </span>
    {%- endif -%}
    <span class="hlt-drawer-trust__text">{{ hlt_trust_text | escape }}</span>
  </p>
{%- endif -%}
